          "source_text_sha256": "a64c49d2b7e318ee6641d526d1eea4066cbd5406293df2b1b4d495e228c73d61",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On July 19, 2015, around midnight, two people observed through binoculars a line of several orange lights in the sky. The objects shimmered, and the whole scene resembled a formation flight moving from West to East. One witness noticed a last light quickly joining the others. Only one testimony was collected. Given the elements gathered in the investigation report (see attached), namely: - the identical orange color to that of lanterns. - the behavior identical to that of objects subject to no or weak wind (moderate speed). - the short observation duration (around 1 minute), compatible with the lifespan of lanterns. - the date: a Sunday evening, compatible with those propitious for the organization of lantern releases on celebrations. - the number compatible with that of lanterns launched in quantity. - the illusion of acceleration and disappearance caused by the extinction of lanterns or entry into the cloud layer. - the absence of noise. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\" as a very probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "9d8df80ba5df808ac90c72a44956735d5209224568bbad6928580dee3dcd62fa"
        }
      ],
